sigharvest is a tool: this repository does not contain or redistribute third-party Sigma rules. The rules it
collects stay the property of their authors and are governed by the licence of the repository (or file) they come
from, for example the Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 for SigmaHQ rules, or MIT, Apache-2.0, GPL and others.

- Every exported rule, zip and release pack carries its own NOTICE.md and per-rule source, author and licence
  information (manifest.jsonl, ATTRIBUTION.md); query exports keep an attribution line for every converted rule.
- The licence of each configured source is recorded in sources/*.yaml and shown by `sigharvest sources list`, on
  every rule page and in release metadata. Rules from repositories without a licence are linked, never shipped.
- Release packs are split by licence family (permissive and copyleft); see docs/releases.md.

Check the licence of each rule before you redistribute it or the queries converted from it.

